Add native VS Code workspace for rumpelpod

Add a workspace extension that switches pods from an Activity Bar view.
Attach agent and shell sessions in sidebar xterm terminals. Show pod
changes in native VS Code multi-diff editors. Run CLI commands under a
packaged node-pty binding. Pod creation, lifecycle output, and
interactive sessions share the CLI's established terminal behavior.

Deny Rust warnings through inherited workspace lints so pipeline builds
preserve the target-specific flags required for runnable musl binaries.

Generate editor protocol typings from the daemon's list and review
snapshots plus live invalidation events. Have the extension consume
those endpoints directly over the Unix socket without JSON CLI modes or
an event subprocess. Keep the extension-specific rumpel core surface
limited to type exports; use the daemon and CLI lifecycle behavior
shared with main.
Do not retain the abandoned daemon PTY streaming routes or API.

Publish separate Linux x64, Linux arm64, and macOS arm64 VSIX assets.
Build them in existing platform jobs. Preserve the multi-binary rumpel
tarball and installer. Build Linux bindings in a pinned Bullseye image.
Reject bindings above the supported glibc baseline. Keep normal pipeline
extension checks local so they do not start nested Docker builds.
Declare extension development dependencies with npm's latest dist-tag,
apart from the VS Code type range that its packager requires. Use the
lockfile as the reproducible source of exact versions. Refresh that
graph to the latest stable direct dependencies and patched transitive
releases.

Provide a loopback-only live code-server workspace backed by a small
anyhow demo repository and lingering user services. Run demo pods as a
non-root user because Claude rejects its permission bypass under root.
Persist only allowlisted agent credentials for those services. Install
no daemon service in the image: the first pipeline run installs its
freshly built native daemon and cross-architecture pod payloads after
systemd is available. Let browser VS Code start independently and
reconnect when that daemon appears. Let CI boot mask the browser
service. Use the same complete devcontainer image in development and CI,
and report startup logs when its entrypoint fails. Pin the arm64
code-server archive to its published digest. Keep the timing-sensitive
Playwright test available only through the explicit ignored-test flag.
Keep a bounded terminal cache per pod so scrollback survives pod
switches while parser and mouse state remain isolated. Keep SSH
integration fixtures independent of ambient agents.
